% References for paper/draft.md.
%
% Provenance: every arXiv entry below was generated directly from the
% arXiv API on 2026-08-27 — author lists, titles and years are verbatim
% from that service, not from memory. (This matters: a first pass written
% from memory got four author lists wrong, including two that share a
% first author with a different paper.) The journal entries were resolved
% against Crossref the same day, with volume, issue, pages and DOI as
% returned.
%
% The four entries Crossref and arXiv could not resolve — two books and
% two sets of conference proceedings, which those services index
% patchily — were resolved on 2026-08-27 against DBLP (the proceedings,
% which supplied the page ranges) and Open Library (the books, which
% supplied publisher and ISBN). No entry in this file rests on
% recollection.
%
% Two gotchas found while doing that, worth leaving here:
%
% Open Library's SEARCH endpoint omits the subtitle field; its
% /isbn/<isbn>.json endpoint carries it. Plate (2003)'s subtitle
% "Distributed Representation for Cognitive Structures" looked
% unconfirmable through search and is confirmed through the ISBN
% record, across all three of the book's ISBNs. Kanerva (1988) really
% has no subtitle, checked the same way.
%
% The two booktitle ordinals here were also written from memory and are
% also now verified against DBLP's proceedings records: NIPS volume 20
% is the Twenty-First Annual Conference, Vancouver, December 2007; and
% CogSci 2019 is the 41st Annual Meeting (DBLP spells it "41th").


